Developed a multi-agent AI banking assistant using Spring Boot, LangGraph4j, and Azure OpenAI, orchestrating
Supervisor, Account, Transaction, and Payment Agents for intelligent request routing and task delegation.
• Architected a scalable microservices ecosystem with Spring Cloud Gateway as a unified entry point, Eureka for ser
vice discovery, Spring Cloud LoadBalancer for request distribution, and Config Server for centralized configuration
management.
• Strengthened system resilience by integrating Resilience4j circuit breakers, retries, and timeouts, ensuring graceful
degradation and fault isolation across inter-service communication.
• Leveraged Redis for caching and shared session/conversation state, and Apache Kafka for asynchronous, event
driven communication across payment and transaction workflows.
• Integrated MCP to connect AI agents with core banking services, Azure Document Intelligence for automated
invoice data extraction, and a RAG pipeline for context-aware, grounded responses; containerized all services with
Docker for scalable deployment.
